[{:db/id 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9509d4b2-8f43-5f25-8917-81a3d5d9b04d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9509d4b2-8f43-5f25-8917-81a3d5d9b04d" :question/id #uuid "9509d4b2-8f43-5f25-8917-81a3d5d9b04d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33195" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(0,1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed6bca43-1900-5519-94be-29cc1bb55d43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed6bca43-1900-5519-94be-29cc1bb55d43" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed6bca43-1900-5519-94be-29cc1bb55d43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c899f30d-448a-55d6-a220-50efc27da551" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88b7b35b-b8a9-55fa-b177-e46dd3a1176a" "answer-54c2e93d-88d9-55e5-8da7-a7c8857c95a2" "answer-865e5880-5d6c-5eb8-b605-32023bca731a" "answer-c899f30d-448a-55d6-a220-50efc27da551" "answer-f42a4087-cff6-5d2b-9264-832562c287ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88b7b35b-b8a9-55fa-b177-e46dd3a1176a" :answer/id #uuid "88b7b35b-b8a9-55fa-b177-e46dd3a1176a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54c2e93d-88d9-55e5-8da7-a7c8857c95a2" :answer/id #uuid "54c2e93d-88d9-55e5-8da7-a7c8857c95a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-865e5880-5d6c-5eb8-b605-32023bca731a" :answer/id #uuid "865e5880-5d6c-5eb8-b605-32023bca731a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c899f30d-448a-55d6-a220-50efc27da551" :answer/id #uuid "c899f30d-448a-55d6-a220-50efc27da551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f42a4087-cff6-5d2b-9264-832562c287ce" :answer/id #uuid "f42a4087-cff6-5d2b-9264-832562c287ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393043 :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-5,-2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,3,4⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-68a08d63-69d2-59f4-855e-ab9c40ae1bca" :activity/id #uuid "68a08d63-69d2-59f4-855e-ab9c40ae1bca" :activity/title "The Vector Equation of a Plane" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049436 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3ecf110e-e7e0-5add-b305-ad1bf6c365c5" "step-55812343-3b60-5de3-98f2-95ffd7bd0ddb" "step-0ecb2ec2-22d0-5b28-bc73-c57c70725e45" "step-2c8b595f-b1a8-514e-9b95-bb539ab93fc0" "step-376b1716-abbb-51bb-97e6-b6e06c8b7140"] :activity/first-step "step-3ecf110e-e7e0-5add-b305-ad1bf6c365c5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3ecf110e-e7e0-5add-b305-ad1bf6c365c5" :step/id #uuid "3ecf110e-e7e0-5add-b305-ad1bf6c365c5" :step/content "question-9509d4b2-8f43-5f25-8917-81a3d5d9b04d" :step/next "step-55812343-3b60-5de3-98f2-95ffd7bd0ddb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-55812343-3b60-5de3-98f2-95ffd7bd0ddb" :step/id #uuid "55812343-3b60-5de3-98f2-95ffd7bd0ddb" :step/content 17592186393029 :step/next "step-0ecb2ec2-22d0-5b28-bc73-c57c70725e45" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0ecb2ec2-22d0-5b28-bc73-c57c70725e45" :step/id #uuid "0ecb2ec2-22d0-5b28-bc73-c57c70725e45" :step/content 17592186338831 :step/next "step-2c8b595f-b1a8-514e-9b95-bb539ab93fc0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c8b595f-b1a8-514e-9b95-bb539ab93fc0" :step/id #uuid "2c8b595f-b1a8-514e-9b95-bb539ab93fc0" :step/content 17592186393043 :step/next "step-376b1716-abbb-51bb-97e6-b6e06c8b7140" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-376b1716-abbb-51bb-97e6-b6e06c8b7140" :step/id #uuid "376b1716-abbb-51bb-97e6-b6e06c8b7140" :step/content 17592186262855 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
